WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.789
Coils.

2
00:00:00.949 --> 00:00:03.875
A coil pot is built from rolled sausages of clay.

3
00:00:04.035 --> 00:00:09.933
Each one is scored, slipped and smoothed into the one below, so the rings become a single wall.

4
00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:12.694
Turn the pot as you build and it grows evenly.

5
00:00:13.394 --> 00:00:14.276
Slabs.

6
00:00:14.436 --> 00:00:16.619
Roll the clay flat and you have a slab.

7
00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:21.562
Cut it and you get flat sides and sharp corners: tiles, boxes, little houses.

8
00:00:21.722 --> 00:00:24.230
A slab pot is built like a piece of carpentry.

9
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.230
Where the weight goes.

10
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:32.845
The bottom of a tall pot carries everything above it, so the lower coils are made thicker and given time to firm up.

11
00:00:33.005 --> 00:00:36.953
The part under the most stress is always the part you build strongest.

12
00:00:37.653 --> 00:00:39.046
A jar with a job.

13
00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:51.605
The two-handled jars of ancient Greece were built for carrying oil and water: a narrow neck so nothing slops out, a wide belly to hold a lot, two handles because a full jar is heavy, and a foot to stand on.
